ographer.  \nVideographer is in position 1 → adjacent person is position 2.  \nSo Pakistani must be in position 2 (since position 1 is videographer, and Pakistani ≠ videographer — because each person has unique attributes, and the constraint says “the person who is Pakistani is on the immediate left/right of the person who is a videographer” — implying they are different people).\n\nTherefore:\n\n> Position 2: Nationality = Pakistani  \n> Position 1: Nationality = Nigerian\n\nNow let’s answer the questions:\n\n1. **What is the job of the person who is Pakistani?**  \n   Pakistani is in position 2 → job = freelancer\n\n2. **What is the movie genre of the person who is Pakistani?**  \n   Pakistani is in position 2 → movie genre = animation\n\n3. **What movie genre does the person in position 1 watch?**  \n   Position 1 → thriller\n\n4. **At what position is the person who is a videographer?**  \n   Position 1\n\nSo answers in order:\n\n1. freelancer  \n2. animation  \n3. thriller  \n4. 1\n\nFinal answer format: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>freelancer, animation, thriller, 1</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.12692900002002716}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.023355737328529358}, {"token": " given", "logprob": -0.3868725597858429}, {"token": ":\n\n", "logprob": -0.14301663637161255}, {"token": "-", "logprob": -0.001994288759306073}, {"token": " Two", "logprob": -0.12748512625694275}, {"token": " people", "logprob": -7.70062324590981e-05}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.0029937471263110638}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00867254938930273}, {"token": " line", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.06198979914188385}, {"token": " numbered", "logprob": -0.7072899341583252}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0686730220913887}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " (", "logprob": -0.0008079125545918941}, {"token": "left", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": ")"